# Add New Calculator

When the user says "新增一个计算器页面" or similar, follow this automated workflow.

## Step 0: Read Plan & Pick Next Item

1. Read `.cursor/plans/calculators.json`
2. Find the first item with `"status": "pending"`
3. Use that item's data (slug, title, shortTitle, category, keywords) as the work target
4. Announce: "Working on: [title]"

## Step 1: Register in Data

Add the calculator to `src/lib/calculators.ts` array:

```typescript
{
  slug: "[from plan]",
  title: "[from plan]",
  shortTitle: "[from plan]",
  description: "[write 50-160 char description targeting the keywords from plan]",
  category: "[from plan]",
  relatedCalculators: ["slug1", "slug2", "slug3"],  // 3-4 semantically related calculators
  relatedGuides: ["guide-slug1", "guide-slug2"],     // 0-3 related guide articles (if any exist)
}
```

Choose `relatedCalculators` based on topic proximity (same financial domain, complementary tools). Choose `relatedGuides` from existing guides in `src/lib/guides.ts` that reference or relate to this calculator's topic.

Add a corresponding SVG icon to `src/components/Icons.tsx` in the `iconMap`.

## Step 2: Create Calculator Directory

Create `src/app/calculators/[slug]/` with three files:

### page.tsx (route entry)

```typescript
import type { Metadata } from "next";
import { getCalculator } from "@/lib/calculators";
import { site } from "@/lib/site";
import { CalculatorShell } from "@/components/CalculatorShell";
import { [Name]Calculator } from "./[Name]Calculator";
import { [Name]Article } from "./[Name]Article";

const calc = getCalculator("[slug]")!;

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: calc.title,
  description: calc.description,
  openGraph: { title: `${calc.title} | ${site.name}`, description: calc.description, type: "website" },
};

export default function [Name]Page() {
  return (
    <CalculatorShell calculator={calc} article={<[Name]Article />}>
      <[Name]Calculator />
    </CalculatorShell>
  );
}
```

### [Name]Calculator.tsx (interactive widget)

- Must be a `"use client"` component
- Use `InputField` component from `@/components/InputField`
- All calculation logic in a `useMemo` hook
- Format currency with `toLocaleString("en-US", { style: "currency", currency: "USD" })`
- Show results in colored cards (bg-brand-50, bg-accent-50, bg-ink-100)
- Include data tables or breakdowns where applicable
- NO emoji anywhere
- Accept optional `defaults?: Record<string, string>` prop for variant pages

### [Name]Article.tsx (educational content)

- Must `import Link from "next/link"` and include internal links
- Must contain 800-1200 words minimum
- Structure: Infographic → How it works → Key concepts → Concrete case study → Comparison table → Tips → FAQ (3-5 questions)
- Include at least one infographic image generated with kie-image:

```bash
# 1. Generate
node ~/.cursor/skills/kie-image/generate.mjs "[descriptive prompt for infographic, clean minimal style, white background, blue/green color scheme, professional financial data visualization, no decorative elements]" "3:2" --resolution 2K

# 2. Download + resize + convert to webp
curl -o /tmp/calc-infographic.png "[result_url]"
sips --resampleWidth 1200 /tmp/calc-infographic.png --out /tmp/calc-resized.png
cwebp -q 80 /tmp/calc-resized.png -o public/images/[slug]-infographic.webp
rm /tmp/calc-infographic.png /tmp/calc-resized.png
```

Embed with next/image (1200x800 for 3:2 ratio):
```tsx
<Image src="/images/[slug]-infographic.webp" alt="[descriptive]" width={1200} height={800} className="rounded-lg border border-ink-200" />
```

Content requirements:
- At least one concrete case study with a named persona and specific dollar amounts
- At least one comparison table (e.g. different scenarios, rates, terms)
- NO generic filler — every paragraph must provide actionable insight
- NO emoji anywhere
- 2-3 inline `<Link>` elements to related calculators (from relatedCalculators field)
- 1-2 inline `<Link>` elements to related guides (from relatedGuides field)
- Links should flow naturally within paragraphs, not be dumped in one spot
- Use className="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-800 font-medium" for all internal links

## Step 3: Verify Build

Run `npm run build` and confirm the new page appears.

## Step 4: Commit & Push

```bash
git add -A && git commit -m "Add [calculator title]" && git push
```

## Step 5: Update Plan Progress

Update `.cursor/plans/calculators.json`: change the item's status from `"pending"` to `"done"` and add `"completedAt": "[ISO date]"`.

## Quality Checklist

- [ ] Calculator logic uses correct financial formula
- [ ] All inputs have sensible defaults
- [ ] Results update reactively as user types
- [ ] `relatedCalculators` and `relatedGuides` populated in calculators.ts entry
- [ ] Article has 800+ words with unique case study and comparison table
- [ ] Article contains 2-3 inline Link elements to related calculators
- [ ] Article contains 1-2 inline Link elements to related guides
- [ ] At least 1 infographic image generated and embedded
- [ ] No emoji used anywhere
- [ ] SVG icon added to Icons.tsx iconMap
- [ ] Build passes with no errors
- [ ] Git committed and pushed
- [ ] Plan JSON updated with "done" status
